Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.00,0:00:09.72,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,Hello everybody in this video we're
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.72,0:00:11.76,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,taking a slightly different approach to
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.76,0:00:13.72,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,interesting facts about Windows
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.28,0:00:16.48,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,This is the first time in a couple of years I'm
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.48,0:00:18.20,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,showing you cool things about Windows. So
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.20,0:00:19.62,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,I wanted it to be special
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.46,0:00:21.80,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,So this is the first time I'm
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.80,0:00:23.30,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,narrating this kind of video
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.61,0:00:26.22,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,and I've also permanently switched editing software
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.56,0:00:28.42,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,I'm now using the DaVinci Resolve
Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.15,0:00:30.75,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,Pretty unusual experience from me
Dialogue: 0,0:00:31.30,0:00:33.04,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,and I'm still a beginner so any
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.04,0:00:35.39,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,feedback in the comments down below would be welcome
Dialogue: 0,0:00:36.49,0:00:37.77,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,But anyway let's begin!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.13,0:00:41.52,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,Welcome to 11 interesting facts about Windows 11
Dialogue: 0,0:00:42.48,0:00:45.40,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,starting with number 11 the black screen of death
Dialogue: 0,0:00:46.12,0:00:49.08,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,We're going to countown just like in the previous episodes
Dialogue: 0,0:00:50.13,0:00:52.32,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,In the past we've seen the green screen of death
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.34,0:00:54.46,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,the color choice for The Insider builds
Dialogue: 0,0:00:54.87,0:00:57.76,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,the rare undocumented red screen of death which
Dialogue: 0,0:00:57.76,0:01:01.38,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,was likely actually a blue hu shifted due to graphical issues
Dialogue: 0,0:01:01.95,0:01:04.48,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,but the black screen of death was something new and
Dialogue: 0,0:01:04.48,0:01:07.99,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,unexpected with the windows 11 leak way back in 2021
Dialogue: 0,0:01:08.45,0:01:10.60,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,If we quickly hop over to the build
Dialogue: 0,0:01:10.63,0:01:13.66,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,22000 and kill a system process
Dialogue: 0,0:01:13.69,0:01:16.86,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,We'll see a black screen of death with a blue QR code
Dialogue: 0,0:01:17.20,0:01:18.09,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,beautiful
Dialogue: 0,0:01:18.59,0:01:22.08,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,just like most initial Windows 11 cosmetic changes this one was
Dialogue: 0,0:01:22.08,0:01:25.24,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,also incomplete being applied haphazardly
Dialogue: 0,0:01:26.05,0:01:30.30,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,Microsoft never commented on such a seemingly fundamental cosmetic change
Dialogue: 0,0:01:30.85,0:01:32.52,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,and a couple builds later
Dialogue: 0,0:01:32.52,0:01:34.30,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,the screen became blue again
Dialogue: 0,0:01:34.92,0:01:37.29,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,not that anyone cared from what I've seen
Dialogue: 0,0:01:37.55,0:01:39.20,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,There wasn't any backlash
Dialogue: 0,0:01:39.53,0:01:41.40,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,and it wasn't big news for some reason
Dialogue: 0,0:01:41.48,0:01:43.24,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,the community was indifferent
Dialogue: 0,0:01:44.02,0:01:47.68,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,it might have been a failed experiment it can't be coincidental
Dialogue: 0,0:01:47.68,0:01:50.12,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,the first build with a black screen of death
Dialogue: 0,0:01:50.12,0:01:52.88,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,also started a revamped log on UI
Dialogue: 0,0:01:52.88,0:01:54.26,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,with a black root color
Dialogue: 0,0:01:54.97,0:01:58.12,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,The Blue check screen color was likely intended to complement
Dialogue: 0,0:01:58.14,0:02:00.58,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,the new root color of the shutdown screen
Dialogue: 0,0:02:01.11,0:02:02.56,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,and it was pretty thought through
Dialogue: 0,0:02:02.56,0:02:04.52,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,because the acronym hadn't changed
Dialogue: 0,0:02:04.52,0:02:05.77,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,whether it's blue or black
Dialogue: 0,0:02:05.96,0:02:07.75,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,it's still a sord
Dialogue: 0,0:02:08.35,0:02:12.60,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,number 10 you can easily install Windows 11 without  bloatware
Dialogue: 0,0:02:14.15,0:02:17.56,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,Installing Windows on your computer brings you candy crushed
Dialogue: 0,0:02:17.63,0:02:22.08,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,Facebook and other unwanted win UI software being polite
Dialogue: 0,0:02:22.37,0:02:23.52,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,here the key problem is that
Dialogue: 0,0:02:23.52,0:02:25.77,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,Windows is essentially free
Dialogue: 0,0:02:25.95,0:02:27.49,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,making you the product
Dialogue: 0,0:02:27.65,0:02:31.88,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,So they're profiting off of you by installing spored garbage onto your computer
Dialogue: 0,0:02:32.11,0:02:36.03,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,there are two ways to install Windows and not get your face candy crushed
Dialogue: 0,0:02:36.80,0:02:40.63,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,the first one is to get an iot Enterprise version of Windows 11
Dialogue: 0,0:02:41.24,0:02:44.09,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,iot stands for The Internet of Things by the way
Dialogue: 0,0:02:44.54,0:02:46.60,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,that version is intended for Niche
Dialogue: 0,0:02:46.60,0:02:49.35,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,Enterprise devices performing automated tasks
Dialogue: 0,0:02:49.37,0:02:52.73,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,using Windows instead of Linux for some reason
Dialogue: 0,0:02:53.03,0:02:56.07,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,Since There is close to non-user input on such devices
Dialogue: 0,0:02:56.38,0:02:59.40,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,Microsoft have no reason to push sponsored apps
Dialogue: 0,0:02:59.40,0:03:03.41,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,and therefore therefore that version is super lean and tidy
Dialogue: 0,0:03:04.16,0:03:06.08,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,another benefit of using iot
Dialogue: 0,0:03:06.11,0:03:08.70,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,Enterprise is ultra extended support
Dialogue: 0,0:03:09.05,0:03:11.64,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,in fact the iot Enterprise Windows versions
Dialogue: 0,0:03:11.64,0:03:13.72,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,are supported the longest
Dialogue: 0,0:03:13.95,0:03:16.64,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,you can also still activate iot Enterprise once and
Dialogue: 0,0:03:16.64,0:03:19.21,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,for all using the hardware ID method
Dialogue: 0,0:03:19.56,0:03:21.12,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,there are no artificial Hardware
Dialogue: 0,0:03:21.12,0:03:22.95,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,requirements during the setup
Dialogue: 0,0:03:23.21,0:03:25.40,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,the Telemetry is turned off by default
Dialogue: 0,0:03:25.71,0:03:27.84,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,it does not pre-allocate space for updates
Dialogue: 0,0:03:27.84,0:03:29.61,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,and temporary files and Storage
Dialogue: 0,0:03:29.98,0:03:32.16,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,the samba client is much more compatible
Dialogue: 0,0:03:32.16,0:03:34.11,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,with the older versions of Windows
Dialogue: 0,0:03:34.33,0:03:36.12,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,it does not randomly start encrypting your
Dialogue: 0,0:03:36.12,0:03:37.82,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,system Drive using bitLocker
Dialogue: 0,0:03:38.04,0:03:42.10,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,you can use device Update Center and much much more
Dialogue: 0,0:03:42.71,0:03:45.07,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,it's just so freaking good
Dialogue: 0,0:03:45.25,0:03:47.32,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,that version of Windows is what Windows is
Dialogue: 0,0:03:47.32,0:03:49.24,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,supposed to be for consumers
Dialogue: 0,0:03:49.63,0:03:52.12,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,but the consumers are the product and the
Dialogue: 0,0:03:52.12,0:03:54.02,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,Enterprises are their customers
Dialogue: 0,0:03:54.16,0:03:55.64,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,so that all makes sense
Dialogue: 0,0:03:55.78,0:03:58.40,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,don't be a product be a customer instead
Dialogue: 0,0:03:58.78,0:04:02.57,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,the only drawback is that Microsoft Edge is not uninstallable
Dialogue: 0,0:04:03.10,0:04:05.44,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,but there's a trick if you don't like edge
Dialogue: 0,0:04:05.93,0:04:08.84,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,thanks to the euro commission you can uninstall Edge in the
Dialogue: 0,0:04:08.84,0:04:12.40,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,euro region on a nonot Enterprise version
Dialogue: 0,0:04:12.96,0:04:14.84,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,switching Windows versions can be done
Dialogue: 0,0:04:14.84,0:04:16.55,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,via changing the product key
Dialogue: 0,0:04:16.71,0:04:18.91,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,the region can be changed through settings
Dialogue: 0,0:04:19.18,0:04:23.12,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,you're not going to lose any iot perks I mentioned if you switch back after
Dialogue: 0,0:04:23.12,0:04:25.47,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,uninstalling the godforsaken browser
Dialogue: 0,0:04:25.92,0:04:29.88,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,if you guys want I can make a separate video showing how to configure the iot
Dialogue: 0,0:04:29.88,0:04:31.96,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,the Enterprise version to be perfect
Dialogue: 0,0:04:32.69,0:04:35.56,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,you can find the download link in the description below
Dialogue: 0,0:04:36.22,0:04:40.62,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,I'm just afraid they're going to start pushing garbage in that version as well if it becomes mainstream
Dialogue: 0,0:04:41.14,0:04:44.20,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,but I mean we've got 10 years left right
Dialogue: 0,0:04:44.68,0:04:48.31,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,the second option is to set a specific region during the setup
Dialogue: 0,0:04:48.72,0:04:52.88,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,you got to select English with a world in the parentheses
Dialogue: 0,0:04:52.88,0:04:55.21,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,to get a relatively clean version of Windows
Dialogue: 0,0:04:55.73,0:04:59.93,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,you'll not get the iot experience with its infinite perks this way
Dialogue: 0,0:05:00.12,0:05:02.99,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,but you'll get a clean install without any bloat
Dialogue: 0,0:05:03.32,0:05:06.37,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,until you set the region that's when the floodgates open
Dialogue: 0,0:05:06.62,0:05:09.31,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,Microsoft hates customers
Dialogue: 0,0:05:09.77,0:05:13.24,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,or and the Microsoft store will not work until you set the region
Dialogue: 0,0:05:13.37,0:05:15.66,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,so yeah that's the drawback
Dialogue: 0,0:05:15.90,0:05:19.36,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,the first option is so much better just go iot
Dialogue: 0,0:05:19.36,0:05:21.38,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,don't waste your time and nerves
Dialogue: 0,0:05:22.22,0:05:25.71,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,number nine making windows more verbose
Dialogue: 0,0:05:26.31,0:05:29.67,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,anytime I install Windows the first tweaks I apply
Dialogue: 0,0:05:29.82,0:05:35.16,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,are enabling the verbose status and enabling the blue screen display parameters
Dialogue: 0,0:05:35.47,0:05:38.68,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,I have no idea why that's not enabled by default
Dialogue: 0,0:05:38.91,0:05:42.28,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,I know the verbose status is enabled by default on Windows server
Dialogue: 0,0:05:42.38,0:05:45.84,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,but the blue screen has become less and less informative as time went
Dialogue: 0,0:05:45.99,0:05:50.33,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,so we got to fix that what I mean by that is that since Windows 8
Dialogue: 0,0:05:50.37,0:05:53.38,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,the blue screen no longer shows the bug check parameters
Dialogue: 0,0:05:53.59,0:05:57.03,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,limiting you to the human readable Bug check code and numeration
Dialogue: 0,0:05:57.61,0:05:59.87,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,sometimes that's just not enough
Dialogue: 0,0:06:00.03,0:06:02.20,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,I don't know why they removed that by default
Dialogue: 0,0:06:02.38,0:06:05.44,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,it's almost as if the bug check is supposed to look nice
Dialogue: 0,0:06:05.44,0:06:06.68,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,instead of giving you as much
Dialogue: 0,0:06:06.68,0:06:09.23,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,information about the crash as possible in the moment
Dialogue: 0,0:06:09.87,0:06:15.09,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,the fix is simple enough you have to set two registry values shown on the screen
Dialogue: 0,0:06:15.35,0:06:17.88,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,after you've set those puppies windows will actually tell
Dialogue: 0,0:06:17.88,0:06:19.12,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,you what's going on
Dialogue: 0,0:06:19.48,0:06:22.48,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,the verbose shutdown screen is also pretty important because
Dialogue: 0,0:06:22.48,0:06:24.40,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,sometimes a service just doesn't want to
Dialogue: 0,0:06:24.40,0:06:26.08,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,exit and you're just stuck there looking
Dialogue: 0,0:06:26.08,0:06:29.48,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,at restarting or shutting down
Dialogue: 0,0:06:29.90,0:06:32.16,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,what's that obsessive compulsion with hiding
Dialogue: 0,0:06:32.16,0:06:34.40,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,extra information a user might genuinely
Dialogue: 0,0:06:34.40,0:06:36.06,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,need to debug Windows
Dialogue: 0,0:06:36.54,0:06:37.74,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,something happened
Dialogue: 0,0:06:38.04,0:06:39.49,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,God I really hate that
Dialogue: 0,0:06:40.80,0:06:44.58,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,number 8 emergency restart
Dialogue: 0,0:06:45.21,0:06:48.43,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,Windows is full of mysteries and hidden functionality
Dialogue: 0,0:06:48.69,0:06:52.23,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,one such feature is called an emergency restart
Dialogue: 0,0:06:52.50,0:06:55.44,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,it's pretty useful of Windows randomly craps itself
Dialogue: 0,0:06:55.44,0:06:56.97,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,and of course it's hidden
Dialogue: 0,0:06:57.47,0:07:00.76,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,to find it you must enter security option AKA press
Dialogue: 0,0:07:00.76,0:07:02.30,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,Control Alt Delete
Dialogue: 0,0:07:02.71,0:07:07.78,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,in there at the bottom right you'll find the power options button
Dialogue: 0,0:07:09.01,0:07:10.28,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,if you just click on the power
Dialogue: 0,0:07:10.28,0:07:14.68,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,icon you'll get all the generics like sleep shutdown restart
Dialogue: 0,0:07:15.68,0:07:17.40,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,to get to the emergency restart
Dialogue: 0,0:07:17.40,0:07:20.28,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,menu you have to hold down
Dialogue: 0,0:07:20.28,0:07:24.18,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,control and only then click on the power options
Dialogue: 0,0:07:25.93,0:07:27.44,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,click okay to immediately
Dialogue: 0,0:07:27.44,0:07:32.55,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,restart any unsaved data will be lost use this only as a last resort
Dialogue: 0,0:07:33.49,0:07:36.11,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,if only you guys knew this existed right
Dialogue: 0,0:07:37.66,0:07:41.32,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,for a moment this was a thing since Windows Vista
Dialogue: 0,0:07:42.35,0:07:45.20,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,can also hold control and press
Dialogue: 0,0:07:45.22,0:07:48.48,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,shutdown there you go emergency restart
Dialogue: 0,0:07:52.86,0:07:54.80,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,works just as well
Dialogue: 0,0:07:55.74,0:07:59.60,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,number 7 the f8 boot options
Dialogue: 0,0:08:00.44,0:08:03.24,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,I cannot describe how abysmal entering
Dialogue: 0,0:08:03.24,0:08:06.04,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,the safe mode has become after Windows 7
Dialogue: 0,0:08:06.36,0:08:07.88,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,you have to hold shift at the right
Dialogue: 0,0:08:07.88,0:08:09.88,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,moment for a certain period of time to
Dialogue: 0,0:08:09.88,0:08:11.32,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,then get into troubleshooting and
Dialogue: 0,0:08:11.32,0:08:13.58,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,recovery options which might not even work
Dialogue: 0,0:08:13.93,0:08:15.60,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,to then click 20 buttons to even
Dialogue: 0,0:08:15.60,0:08:17.88,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,have a chance of booting into safe mode
Dialogue: 0,0:08:18.23,0:08:20.45,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,why did you make it so difficult
Dialogue: 0,0:08:20.95,0:08:23.60,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,you have invented the f8 and F10 boot menus
Dialogue: 0,0:08:23.60,0:08:25.20,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,they were just so good
Dialogue: 0,0:08:25.68,0:08:28.06,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,instead you have to get rid of what's consistently
Dialogue: 0,0:08:28.08,0:08:30.04,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,working and super convenient only to
Dialogue: 0,0:08:30.04,0:08:31.96,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,replace it with a subjectively better
Dialogue: 0,0:08:31.96,0:08:34.14,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,looking menu behind 20 buttons
Dialogue: 0,0:08:35.22,0:08:37.24,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,what's your problem Microsoft
Dialogue: 0,0:08:37.24,0:08:39.25,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,why is everything becoming a sord
Dialogue: 0,0:08:39.40,0:08:42.32,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,anyway this is how you enable the f8 boot menu
Dialogue: 0,0:08:42.32,0:08:44.20,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,you'll need a command prompt with admin
