Dialogue: 0,0:16:28.84,0:16:32.43,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,I'm not blaming them I'm surprised this thing works at all
Dialogue: 0,0:16:32.90,0:16:37.32,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,sometimes it breaks not all the time but sometimes
Dialogue: 0,0:16:39.82,0:16:45.60,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,number 3 Windows Explorer purposefully slows down indexing in large folders
Dialogue: 0,0:16:46.63,0:16:50.16,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,NTFS is trash it's a garbage
Dialogue: 0,0:16:50.19,0:16:52.44,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,file system that loses to X for in every
Dialogue: 0,0:16:52.44,0:16:54.73,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,possible aspect including reliability
Dialogue: 0,0:16:55.23,0:16:57.52,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,my hard drive wears off faster thanks to
Dialogue: 0,0:16:57.52,0:17:00.01,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,NTFS and extra fragment that comes with it
Dialogue: 0,0:17:00.90,0:17:04.44,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,Windows should support X4 ZFS btrfs
Dialogue: 0,0:17:04.44,0:17:06.52,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,and everything else out of the box
Dialogue: 0,0:17:06.52,0:17:08.88,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,period it's time for NTFS to go
Dialogue: 0,0:17:08.88,0:17:10.80,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,Microsoft but of of course it's not
Dialogue: 0,0:17:10.80,0:17:12.44,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,going to happen they're like three
Dialogue: 0,0:17:12.44,0:17:15.24,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,unpaid interns working on Windows 4 hours a day
Dialogue: 0,0:17:15.39,0:17:17.20,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,and there is no incentive to improve
Dialogue: 0,0:17:18.57,0:17:25.52,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,but all this aside Windows Explorer is still hardwired to slow file indexing down even further
Dialogue: 0,0:17:26.14,0:17:28.96,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,and I'm not even kidding have you ever wondered why
Dialogue: 0,0:17:28.96,0:17:33.48,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,Windows Explorer takes an obscene amount of time to load a folder with a large amount of files
Dialogue: 0,0:17:34.36,0:17:37.24,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,naturally your first and the final
Dialogue: 0,0:17:37.24,0:17:41.28,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,guess would be that NTFS is garbage and
Dialogue: 0,0:17:41.28,0:17:44.58,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,that's it because you can't do anything about that
Dialogue: 0,0:17:44.95,0:17:49.28,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,and you're not wrong NTFS really struggles with a large file count
Dialogue: 0,0:17:49.28,0:17:52.72,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,but in reality NTFS isn't that garbage
Dialogue: 0,0:17:53.79,0:17:59.04,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,it's Windows Explorer adding salt to the wound by having the automatic Discovery feature enabled by default
Dialogue: 0,0:17:59.91,0:18:01.76,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,what exactly does that do
Dialogue: 0,0:18:02.64,0:18:05.44,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,it changes the view of the folder you're currently in
Dialogue: 0,0:18:05.44,0:18:07.25,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,based on the contents of the folder
Dialogue: 0,0:18:07.57,0:18:11.40,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,that means let's say you have 10,000 video files in a folder
Dialogue: 0,0:18:12.02,0:18:14.96,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,I do have such a folder on my hard drive it's not called
Dialogue: 0,0:18:14.96,0:18:17.04,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,homework by the way don't worry it's a
Dialogue: 0,0:18:17.04,0:18:20.41,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,folder with all my OBS recordings throughout the years
Dialogue: 0,0:18:21.24,0:18:24.48,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,anyway the automatic folder Discovery will determine
Dialogue: 0,0:18:25.12,0:18:28.16,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,it should optimize the Explorer view for video files because
Dialogue: 0,0:18:28.16,0:18:31.17,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,the content are entirely video files
Dialogue: 0,0:18:31.64,0:18:34.88,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,meaning it has to take every single video file
Dialogue: 0,0:18:36.00,0:18:37.37,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,pull the thumbnail out of it
Dialogue: 0,0:18:37.86,0:18:40.86,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,and then draw it 10,000 times
Dialogue: 0,0:18:42.61,0:18:46.03,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,just like that do you hear my hard drive?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:48.62,0:18:52.96,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,oh you probably don't it's going to take more time to load
Dialogue: 0,0:18:53.88,0:18:56.32,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,that's not only horrible for your mental health
Dialogue: 0,0:18:56.61,0:19:00.16,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,that's also horrible for the hard drive it has to spin up for
Dialogue: 0,0:19:00.16,0:19:02.40,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,that seemingly harmless view change
Dialogue: 0,0:19:03.41,0:19:05.69,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,so how do you turn this travesty off
Dialogue: 0,0:19:06.13,0:19:09.81,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,that's an elaborate registry tweak so follow me closely
Dialogue: 0,0:19:10.20,0:19:13.08,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,I'm going to do this on my host because I reinstalled
Dialogue: 0,0:19:13.08,0:19:16.86,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,Windows recently and the windows web search is garbage
Dialogue: 0,0:19:19.89,0:19:22.26,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,and I haven't gotten to apply The tweak yet
Dialogue: 0,0:19:22.74,0:19:25.72,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,making a video after three months of absence would be a good excuse
Dialogue: 0,0:19:25.72,0:19:28.71,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,to do that right I'm sorry guys
Dialogue: 0,0:19:29.36,0:19:33.35,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,anyway in the registry editor we have to open the following registry key
Dialogue: 0,0:19:34.00,0:19:35.12,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,let's navigate towards it
Dialogue: 0,0:19:45.76,0:19:49.60,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,and in here we have two keys
Dialogue: 0,0:19:49.60,0:19:52.57,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,called bags and bagMRU
Dialogue: 0,0:19:53.14,0:19:54.83,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,and we need to delete them both
Dialogue: 0,0:19:56.47,0:20:00.95,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,so quick explanation the bags are the shell views
Dialogue: 0,0:20:01.57,0:20:06.08,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,that's how they're called in Windows so inside you have
Dialogue: 0,0:20:06.08,0:20:08.23,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,like settings for every folder
Dialogue: 0,0:20:08.53,0:20:14.85,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,it's detected before and um you can see sniffed folder type generic
Dialogue: 0,0:20:15.08,0:20:16.60,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,so it couldn't determine
Dialogue: 0,0:20:16.60,0:20:18.80,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,the view exactly for that folder so it
Dialogue: 0,0:20:18.80,0:20:21.28,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,decided to pick the generic View
Dialogue: 0,0:20:22.14,0:20:25.39,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,and it's a tree like structure right here
Dialogue: 0,0:20:25.96,0:20:28.95,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,and on top you have the bagMRU key
Dialogue: 0,0:20:29.36,0:20:33.64,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,which which is basically a Lup table it's like a small database
Dialogue: 0,0:20:36.16,0:20:38.87,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,and it has links to the Bags key
Dialogue: 0,0:20:42.12,0:20:43.96,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,so we have to delete these guys
Dialogue: 0,0:20:43.96,0:20:46.28,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,before we do anything else because these
Dialogue: 0,0:20:46.28,0:20:50.33,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,settings are basically saved in a database
Dialogue: 0,0:20:50.73,0:20:54.08,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,and we have to clean it up we have to drop that database let's go
Dialogue: 0,0:20:54.08,0:20:58.18,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,ahead and delete bags and bagMRU
Dialogue: 0,0:20:58.80,0:21:01.24,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,all right it's not going to break anything
Dialogue: 0,0:21:02.69,0:21:06.07,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,then we have to recreate the Bags key
Dialogue: 0,0:21:07.77,0:21:10.70,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,go ahead create a new key call it bags
Dialogue: 0,0:21:12.24,0:21:15.20,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,then inside the bags we have to
Dialogue: 0,0:21:15.20,0:21:18.58,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,create another key called all folders
Dialogue: 0,0:21:20.73,0:21:22.96,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,that's like a wild card inside
Dialogue: 0,0:21:22.96,0:21:25.00,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,the all folders key you have to create
Dialogue: 0,0:21:25.00,0:21:27.68,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,another sub key called shell
Dialogue: 0,0:21:28.22,0:21:31.16,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,very intuitive I know that's why I'm saying
Dialogue: 0,0:21:31.16,0:21:34.28,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,it's elaborate and inside the Shell Key
Dialogue: 0,0:21:34.28,0:21:39.64,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,you can finally create a string value called folder type
Dialogue: 0,0:21:41.72,0:21:44.52,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,and we'll call it not specified
Dialogue: 0,0:21:47.91,0:21:50.60,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,deleting the bags and the bagMRU Keys
Dialogue: 0,0:21:50.96,0:21:55.76,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,essentially flushed the Explorer view database and now we'll end
Dialogue: 0,0:21:55.76,0:21:58.33,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,up with a generic view for every folder
Dialogue: 0,0:21:58.79,0:22:01.08,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,and setting folder type not specified
Dialogue: 0,0:22:01.08,0:22:05.95,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,here will disable the automatic folder discovery for Windows Explorer
Dialogue: 0,0:22:06.48,0:22:10.36,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,and to apply these settings we have to sign out and sign back into windows
Dialogue: 0,0:22:11.35,0:22:14.00,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,so I signed back into my computer let's go ahead and see what
Dialogue: 0,0:22:14.00,0:22:16.36,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,happened to Windows Explorer after the changes
Dialogue: 0,0:22:17.99,0:22:23.44,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,the window size reset but it's not a big deal we can fix that again
Dialogue: 0,0:22:24.41,0:22:28.46,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,all right let's go ahead and enter the folder
Dialogue: 0,0:22:31.55,0:22:32.95,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,check out the properties
Dialogue: 0,0:22:33.07,0:22:35.35,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,customize and
Dialogue: 0,0:22:37.95,0:22:40.88,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,the folder is now optimized for General items
Dialogue: 0,0:22:41.73,0:22:45.36,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,and it loads in an instant
Dialogue: 0,0:22:45.50,0:22:49.22,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,beautiful that's what we want
Dialogue: 0,0:22:49.43,0:22:51.60,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,before I forget you can also speed up
Dialogue: 0,0:22:51.60,0:22:54.76,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,Explorer by pressing f11 twice and
Dialogue: 0,0:22:54.76,0:22:57.43,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,that's not a joke either so let's go ahead
Dialogue: 0,0:22:58.16,0:22:59.51,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,try the performance
Dialogue: 0,0:23:01.09,0:23:04.80,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,look at this we're browsing through directories
Dialogue: 0,0:23:05.83,0:23:07.02,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,real nice
Dialogue: 0,0:23:08.48,0:23:09.49,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,all right
Dialogue: 0,0:23:11.38,0:23:15.28,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,so now we're going to enter the full screen mode and then exit the full
Dialogue: 0,0:23:15.28,0:23:18.80,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,screen mode Let's see how fast it is now
Dialogue: 0,0:23:20.35,0:23:22.00,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,it's instantaneous
Dialogue: 0,0:23:23.59,0:23:29.19,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,it's not edited it's actually so much faster now
Dialogue: 0,0:23:34.84,0:23:37.45,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,it's absolutely crazy but that's a proven fact
Dialogue: 0,0:23:38.31,0:23:41.10,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,if you enable the full screen mode on Windows Explorer
Dialogue: 0,0:23:41.54,0:23:43.88,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,the directory loading becomes instantaneous
Dialogue: 0,0:23:43.88,0:23:46.30,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,and the Explorer generally starts lagging less
Dialogue: 0,0:23:47.56,0:23:51.64,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,absolutely wild I don't know how they messed it up this bad
Dialogue: 0,0:23:52.45,0:23:58.18,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,number 2 the Windows security questions are plain text
Dialogue: 0,0:23:59.70,0:24:02.44,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,this is one of my favorite go-to facts
Dialogue: 0,0:24:02.44,0:24:06.03,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,when convincing people Microsoft don't actually care about Windows
Dialogue: 0,0:24:06.49,0:24:10.51,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,I've made an entire video about this you can click on the card to watch it
Dialogue: 0,0:24:10.98,0:24:13.92,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,both the security questions and the answers can be
Dialogue: 0,0:24:13.92,0:24:17.20,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,accessed and modified if you have administrator rights
Dialogue: 0,0:24:17.38,0:24:22.67,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,they are stored in a plain text json and coded in little Indian utf16
Dialogue: 0,0:24:22.83,0:24:25.45,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,residing in the Sam registry key
Dialogue: 0,0:24:39.17,0:24:42.56,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,I was thinking for quite a bit and decided to put this fact on top of the
Dialogue: 0,0:24:42.56,0:24:46.54,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,list because of how often it is overlooked and how useful it is
Dialogue: 0,0:24:47.28,0:24:49.20,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,shell commands are otherwise known as shell
Dialogue: 0,0:24:49.20,0:24:52.87,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,shortcuts and windows has a hardcoded set of these
Dialogue: 0,0:24:53.24,0:24:56.08,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,some of them allow you to reach into really tight crevices or
Dialogue: 0,0:24:56.08,0:24:58.73,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,Windows where light doesn't usually shine
Dialogue: 0,0:24:59.36,0:25:01.12,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,there are two types of shell commands
Dialogue: 0,0:25:01.12,0:25:03.00,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,the ones with friendly names attached to
Dialogue: 0,0:25:03.00,0:25:05.86,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,them and the bare CLS ID ones
Dialogue: 0,0:25:06.54,0:25:09.92,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,the former is really easy to remember for instance
Dialogue: 0,0:25:09.92,0:25:14.35,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,let's just open the command prompt and use one of these right now
Dialogue: 0,0:25:19.20,0:25:21.64,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,wow it opens the user startup folder
Dialogue: 0,0:25:22.17,0:25:25.19,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,how convenient let's try another one
Dialogue: 0,0:25:28.73,0:25:30.58,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,that open library list
Dialogue: 0,0:25:31.97,0:25:34.12,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,simple and elegant
Dialogue: 0,0:25:35.10,0:25:36.58,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,it's not rocket science
Dialogue: 0,0:25:36.82,0:25:40.03,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,the latter is where the fun begins
Dialogue: 0,0:25:40.14,0:25:42.72,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,you copy a magic string put it as an argument for
Dialogue: 0,0:25:42.72,0:25:45.08,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,Windows Explorer and have some crazy
Dialogue: 0,0:25:45.08,0:25:48.14,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,window no one has ever seen before open
Dialogue: 0,0:25:48.36,0:25:53.12,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,it's kind of like a loot box if you don't know what the CLS ID represents before pasting it
Dialogue: 0,0:25:54.15,0:25:56.79,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,so let's copy this puppy right here
Dialogue: 0,0:26:02.89,0:26:05.51,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,this opened the window search
Dialogue: 0,0:26:09.28,0:26:10.71,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,what about this one
Dialogue: 0,0:26:13.83,0:26:15.81,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,this open the Run box
Dialogue: 0,0:26:20.51,0:26:21.91,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,let's try this one
Dialogue: 0,0:26:26.45,0:26:30.15,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,it opened the old notification area I can dialogue
Dialogue: 0,0:26:30.51,0:26:33.36,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,and as you can see it's very broken
Dialogue: 0,0:26:35.57,0:26:38.24,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,and so on and so forth uh this
Dialogue: 0,0:26:38.24,0:26:40.00,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,is pretty much god mode oh wait god mode
Dialogue: 0,0:26:41.12,0:26:42.95,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,god mode is actually a shell command
Dialogue: 0,0:26:43.80,0:26:45.84,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,how handy look at
Dialogue: 0,0:26:46.80,0:26:48.88,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,there you go that's the god mode
Dialogue: 0,0:26:48.88,0:26:53.12,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,remember that from Windows 7 used to be so much more useful back then
Dialogue: 0,0:26:53.91,0:26:59.86,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,but when the Windows settings app hasn't superseded the control panel
Dialogue: 0,0:27:02.68,0:27:07.40,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,you can find Shell command lists on the internet there is a lot of them
Dialogue: 0,0:27:07.79,0:27:13.44,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,like a lot anyway I hope you enjoyed this video
Dialogue: 0,0:27:13.44,0:27:16.56,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,I hope to make more and in a faster Pace
Dialogue: 0,0:27:16.56,0:27:20.92,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,uh as I said already I'm a resolve beginner and I don't have much time on
Dialogue: 0,0:27:20.92,0:27:27.60,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,hand so I'm trying my best got many cool ideas I'm finishing University soon
Dialogue: 0,0:27:27.60,0:27:33.92,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,getting my first degree in software engineering pretty hyped looking forward to what life brings
Dialogue: 0,0:27:34.91,0:27:39.86,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,anyway rate the video subscribe if you enjoyed and take care
